From 0983eb128c4235e42c1de2b9e685f0044e1ed0f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 18:40:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06929/11362] [outer-loop] g50t full game clear (L7/7), fix
 apply_g50t_label post-WIN settling bug

Round-12 codex session live-executed the round-11 phase-sync hypothesis for
g50t's right swap pair and reached a genuine GameState.WIN (level 7, the
game's final level per arc3_win_condition_survey n_levels=7). Root-caused
round 11's degenerate/empty-frame false negative: apply_g50t_label's
settling loop re-submitted the same action after a real WIN frame, and the
post-win step returned an empty terminal sentinel that looked like a lost
game. Patched apply_g50t_label to stop on GameState.WIN immediately (both
on the first step and inside the settling loop) instead of polling further.

Independently re-verified 5x fresh via a new resolver priority branch
(g50t levels_reproduced>=7) using the patched apply function: all 5 trials
state=GameState.WIN, level=7, levels_completed=7, win_levels=7,
is_empty()=False. Added regression tests for the stop-on-win fix using a
fake env (no real ARC environment needed).

lf52 round 12 (12th consecutive round on lf52 L7): honest null, banked for
the record -- 100-coordinate far-off-screen sweep and a static-decomposition
alternate-route hypothesis both explored, neither live-executed within
budget. No level change (frontier stays L6).

reproducible_total_levels: 174 -> 175.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
